# Everything below is written by `npx cap sync ios` on every run and is NOT
# committed - the same rule the Android project follows for its equivalents
# (android/.gitignore: capacitor-cordova-android-plugins, the assets copy of
# capacitor.config.json, res/xml/config.xml). These five paths were force-added
# once, which left two copies of the truth: CI always regenerates them before
# it builds, so the committed copies were never what shipped and could go stale
# without anyone noticing. The one source is guidon-app/capacitor.config.json.
# tools/lint-capacitor-config.mjs (check h) fails if any of them is tracked
# again; the iOS workflow fails if a sync changes a file that IS committed
# (CapApp-SPM/Package.swift - the iOS twin of Android's tracked
# capacitor.settings.gradle / app/capacitor.build.gradle).
#
# A fresh clone therefore needs `npm run ios:sync` before Xcode can build: the
# project references capacitor.config.json, config.xml and public/ as bundle
# resources. That was already true for public/.

# Cordova plugins for Capacitor
capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins

# Generated Config files
App/App/capacitor.config.json
App/App/config.xml
